{
  "id": "pro800",
  "name": "Behringer PRO-800",
  "transport": "pro800",
  "source": "No official MIDI spec. SysEx reverse-engineered by Sam (github.com/samstaton/pro800, pro800syx.md) with Defros' firmware-1.4.6 additions (defros/pro800syx-defros.md, April 2026): message format, 7-in-8 packing, patch offsets and the CC table. Patch layout verified by decoding the published example dumps (format 0x6F = 173 bytes).",
  "sysex": {
    "header": [
      240,
      0,
      32,
      50,
      0,
      1,
      36,
      0
    ],
    "notes": "77 lo hi = request slot n (0-399, n = bank*100 + program, lo = n & 7F); reply 78 lo hi <packed>, and the same 78 message sent TO the unit writes that slot. 77 7E 03 = system dump (decoded bytes 5-6 = current program, LSB first). 08 00 = version request, reply 09 00 maj min patch. Packed like DSI: each 7 bytes preceded by one holding their top bits (bit 0 = first byte). Decoded patch: A5 16 61 00, version (6D/6E old, 6F fw 1.3.6+), then 16-bit little-endian continuous params and 1-byte switches; name at 150 (0x6F: fixed 16, 0-padded; older: 0-terminated). Unmodelled bytes (arp mode 149, unison chord 86-93, per-note tuning 94-141, pitch-bend range 171) ride along from the last read."
  },
  "gapMs": 3,
  "setup": [
    "Settings: MIDI channel = the ch picked above.",
    "Settings: send + receive MIDI CC on, so knob moves show up here and edits land on the synth.",
    "Cable both ways: interface out → PRO-800 MIDI in, PRO-800 MIDI out → interface in (or use its USB port).",
    "Firmware 1.3.6 or newer stores 16-character names; older patches still load."
  ],
  "uncertain": [
    "Nothing here is from Behringer: offsets and the CC table come from probing (samstaton/pro800 + Defros).",
    "LFO Range (CC 58) and LFO Osc Target (CC 59) have no panel control on the unit (fw 1.4.5) — MIDI-only, so the editor is the only way to reach them. LFO Range: patch tables say 0 = slow, CC table 'Fast-Slow'; modelled as patch order.",
    "Voice Spread: patch tables say 'On,Off', CC table 'Off-On'. Modelled as 0 = off — direction confirmed on hardware (fw 1.4.5).",
    "LFO Osc Target: bit mask A 0x08 / B 0x10 / VCA 0x20 (Defros; Sam had VCA at 0x40). Treated as one choice of A+B (no bits), A, B or VCA, matching CC 59's four values.",
    "Writing a 78 dump stores straight to flash? Store reads the slot back and compares, so a write that didn't take shows as an error.",
    "Continuous CCs: assumed linear 14-bit (MSB n, LSB per table) over the panel's 0-999."
  ],
